    "['set policy-options policy-statement [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router isis', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'router isis', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper command `set protocols isis interface lo0.0 passive` to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\nrouter isis\\n passive-interface Loopback0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, `passive` indicates the interface won't form adjacencies but will be advertised in IS-IS\\n- In Cisco, `passive-interface` serves the same purpose under the IS-IS routing process\\n- `Loopback0` is the Cisco equivalent of Juniper's `lo0.0` interface\", 'trans_template': 'router isis'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'passive-interface Loopback0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'passive-interface Loopback0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper command `set protocols isis interface lo0.0 passive` to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\nrouter isis\\n passive-interface Loopback0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, `passive` indicates the interface won't form adjacencies but will be advertised in IS-IS\\n- In Cisco, `passive-interface` serves the same purpose under the IS-IS routing process\\n- `Loopback0` is the Cisco equivalent of Juniper's `lo0.0` interface\", 'trans_template': 'passive-interface Loopback0'}]]": 1,
    "['term [parameter2] from protocol [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'route-map redist-static permit 10', 'parent_command': ['router isis'], 'root': 'router isis', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map redist-static permit 10\\n match ip address static\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Cisco, `route-map` is used similarly to Juniper's `policy-statement`\\n- `permit 10` serves the same purpose as `term 1` (with 10 being the sequence number)\\n- `match ip address static` is the Cisco equivalent of `from protocol static`\\n- The implicit action is to permit (accept) the matched routes, just like `then accept` in Juniper\", 'trans_template': 'route-map redist-static permit 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'match ip address static', 'parent_command': ['router isis'], 'root': 'router isis', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map redist-static permit 10\\n match ip address static\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Cisco, `route-map` is used similarly to Juniper's `policy-statement`\\n- `permit 10` serves the same purpose as `term 1` (with 10 being the sequence number)\\n- `match ip address static` is the Cisco equivalent of `from protocol static`\\n- The implicit action is to permit (accept) the matched routes, just like `then accept` in Juniper\", 'trans_template': 'match ip address static'}]]": 1,
